1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:05,800
I can’t tell my family what I want without feeling ungrateful.

2
00:00:08,250 --> 00:00:13,600
Arjun can put the pressure into his own words, privately.

3
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:25,300
Muse Spark is planned, not connected; it could organize themes for Arjun to review. This response is prepared.

4
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:29,700
A prepared reading is offered for him to check.

5
00:00:29,850 --> 00:00:32,100
He chooses “Not quite.”

6
00:00:32,200 --> 00:00:41,000
Arjun enters: “I want time to decide what I want, without someone choosing stay or leave for me.”

7
00:00:41,100 --> 00:00:47,900
The reflection changes to hold his correction. He decides what fits.

8
00:00:48,800 --> 00:00:56,500
He keeps family context in view and sets broader legal results aside.

9
00:01:04,700 --> 00:01:10,000
A prepared fictional account says Ravi had a trusted friend.

10
00:01:10,100 --> 00:01:16,100
Their circumstances differ; Arjun has not said he has someone he trusts.

11
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:30,450
The preview names the Family Expectations group and the alias QuietRiver.

12
00:01:30,500 --> 00:01:33,350
It shows the question, “Could I take time to decide before answering?”

13
00:01:33,400 --> 00:01:35,200
Private reflection is excluded.

14
00:01:35,250 --> 00:01:39,200
Consent is unchecked; he can cancel and keep the draft.

15
00:01:39,300 --> 00:01:41,400
He cancels and keeps the draft. Nothing is sent.

16
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:47,600
For this prepared preview, Arjun keeps one line privately: “I can ask for time before deciding.”
